---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const phone = '+19255550199';
const phoneDisplay = '(925) 555-0199';
---
<Layout 
  title="No Hot Water Concord CA | Water Heater Not Working"
  description="No hot water in Concord, CA? Fast diagnosis for electric and gas water heaters. Element, thermostat, pilot, and breaker issues fixed same day in most cases."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> → Problems → No Hot Water</div>
      <h1>No Hot Water in Concord, CA?</h1>
      <p>Complete loss of hot water is one of the most disruptive home failures. Most causes are diagnosable and repairable the same day.</p>
      <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Get Help Now — {phoneDisplay}</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-block">
      <h2>Quick Checks You Can Do First</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Check the circuit breaker or fuse for electric units.</li>
        <li>Confirm the gas supply valve is open for gas units.</li>
        <li>Look at the pilot light status (gas).</li>
        <li>Make sure the unit has power / gas and the thermostat is set correctly.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If those basics check out, the problem is internal and needs a technician.</p>

      <h2>Most Common Causes We Find</h2>
      <h3>Electric Water Heaters</h3>
      <p>Failed upper or lower heating element, tripped high-limit switch, or faulty thermostat. Elements are the #1 failure and are usually replaced on the first visit.</p>
      <h3>Gas Water Heaters</h3>
      <p>Pilot out, failed thermocouple, dirty pilot orifice, or gas control valve issues. Thermocouple replacement restores hot water in the majority of “pilot won’t stay lit” calls.</p>
      <h3>Tankless Units</h3>
      <p>Error codes related to ignition, flow, or overheating. Scale, blocked inlet filter, or failed sensors are frequent culprits.</p>

      <h2>What to Expect When We Arrive</h2>
      <p>We perform a systematic diagnostic: power/gas verification, element or burner testing, thermostat function, and overall system health. You receive a clear explanation and written price before any repair begins. Most no-hot-water calls are resolved in a single visit.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;text-align:center">
        <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Call for Same-Day Diagnosis</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
